<article class="env-lemma" id="09EG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09EG">Lemma <span data-tag="09EG">15.112.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $G$ be a finite group acting on $R$. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal such that $\sigma (I) \subset I$ for all $\sigma \in G$. Then $R^ G/I^ G \subset (R/I)^ G$ is an integral extension of rings which induces a homeomorphism on spectra and purely inseparable extensions of residue fields. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $I^ G = R^ G \cap I$ it is clear that the map is injective. Lemma <a href="/tag/0BRF" data-tag="0BRF">15.112.1</a> shows that Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/09EF" data-tag="09EF">10.46.11</a> applies. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>